{"name":"Home Plate","hex":"#f7eedb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"home plate","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flat, pentagonal, rubber object placed at the center of the batter's box, which is used as a basis for judging pitched strikes and balls, and the touching of which by a runner advancing from or past third base scores a run."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/home_plate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Home Plate (Mars)","blocks":[{"text":"Home Plate is a plateau roughly 90 metres (300 ft) across within the Columbia Hills, Mars. It is informally named for its similarity in shape to a baseball home plate. Home Plate is a rocky outcrop that appears to show layered features."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/PIA09089-RA3-hirise-closeup_annotated.png/330px-PIA09089-RA3-hirise-closeup_annotated.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Home_Plate_(Mars)","wikidata":"Q1790919"},{"title":"Home Plate (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Home Plate is the fifth album by Bonnie Raitt, released in 1975."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b2/Bonnie_Raitt_-_Home_Plate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Home_Plate_(album)","wikidata":"Q2224536"},{"title":"Baseball field","blocks":[{"text":"A baseball field, also called a ball field or baseball diamond, is the field upon which the game of baseball is played. The term can also be used as a metonym for a baseball park. The term sandlot is sometimes used, although this usually refers to less organized venues for activities like sandlot ball."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Baseball_diamond_marines.jpg/330px-Baseball_diamond_marines.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baseball_field","wikidata":"Q809889"},{"title":"Home","blocks":[{"text":"A home, or domicile, is a space used as a permanent or semi-permanent residence for one or more human occupants, and sometimes various companion animals. Homes provide sheltered spaces, for instance rooms, where domestic activity can be performed such as sleeping, preparing food, eating, and hygiene as well as providing spaces for work and leisure such as remote working, studying, and playing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/SearsHouse115.jpg/330px-SearsHouse115.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Home","wikidata":"Q7743"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Sol594A_P2281_L257atc-A597R1_br2.jpg/500px-Sol594A_P2281_L257atc-A597R1_br2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Sol594A_P2281_L257atc-A597R1_br2.jpg/1280px-Sol594A_P2281_L257atc-A597R1_br2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Sol594A_P2281_L257atc-A597R1_br2.jpg/500px-Sol594A_P2281_L257atc-A597R1_br2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASol594A_P2281_L257atc-A597R1_br2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Home_plate.JPG/120px-Home_plate.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Home_plate.JPG/250px-Home_plate.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Home_plate.JPG/120px-Home_plate.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https:/